When a table cell has a definite max-width, Ladybird caps the
min-content width of the cell at it, in both its outer min-content and
outer max-content widths, and lets a min-width win over both. Gecko’s
GetISizeInfo(), in BasicTableLayoutStrategy, does the same: It lowers
minCoord and prefCoord to a definite max inline size, then applies the
min inline size. Blink’s TableTypes::CreateCellInlineConstraint() also
lowers the cell’s resolved minimum and its content maximum to the
max-width, but applies the max-width after the min-width, so there the
max-width wins when the two conflict.
